The gentleman cultivates these three qualities and is therefore complete.

Book of Documents
“My words accord with what is right and can be put into practice.” Yu said: “Yes! Your words can be brought to fruition.”
Beginning with the family and the state, and extending ultimately throughout the Four Seas.
When people have ability and accomplishments, let them present their achievements; then your state will flourish.
King Wen was indeed able to cultivate harmony in our land of Xia. There were also men such as Guo Shu, Hong Yao, San Yisheng, Tai Dian, and Nangong Kuo. It is further said: “None could come or go [?]; in this they followed the constant teachings.” King Wen diligently extended his virtue to the people of his state. These men likewise gave wholehearted assistance, upheld virtue, and came to understand Heaven’s awe-inspiring power. Thus they made King Wen illustrious, so that his virtue became manifest and its renown reached the Lord on High; thus he received the mandate formerly held by Yin! With these four men, King Wu likewise attained Heaven’s favor.

Book of Odes
In the south are trees with downward-curving branches;
kudzu and climbing vines entwine them.
Joyful is the gentleman;
may blessings bring him peace!
In the south are trees with downward-curving branches;
kudzu and climbing vines cover them.
Joyful is the gentleman;
may blessings sustain him!
In the south are trees with downward-curving branches;
kudzu and climbing vines wind around them.
Joyful is the gentleman;
may blessings bring him fulfillment!

Look upon the Luo River,
its waters broad and deep.
The gentleman has arrived;
blessings and good fortune have gathered upon him …

The gentleman cultivates these three things and is therefore complete.

Book of Documents
“My words accord with what is right and can be put into practice.” Yu said: “Yes! Your words, when put into practice, can yield accomplishments.”

Begin with the household and the state, and extend ultimately throughout the Four Seas.

When people possess ability and competence, enable them to offer their accomplishments, and your state will flourish.

King Wen was indeed able to cultivate harmony throughout our land of Xia because he had men such as Guo Shu, Hong Yao, San Yisheng, Tai Dian, and Nangong Kuo. It is further said: “Unable to come and go, they nevertheless guided people through these enduring teachings [?].” King Wen tirelessly extended his virtue to the people of his state. These men, too, gave him wholehearted assistance, upheld virtue, and came to understand Heaven’s awe-inspiring power. They thus made King Wen illustrious, so that his virtue became manifest and its influence was heard of by the Lord on High. Thus he received the mandate previously held by Yin! Through these four men, King Wu likewise attained Heaven’s favor.

Book of Odes
In the south are trees with downward-curving branches;
kudzu and other vines entwine them.
Joyful is the lord;
may blessings bring him peace.
In the south are trees with downward-curving branches;
kudzu and other vines cover them.
Joyful is the lord;
may blessings sustain him.
In the south are trees with downward-curving branches;
kudzu and other vines coil around them.
Joyful is the lord;
may blessings bring him fulfillment.

Look at the Luo River,
its waters vast and flowing.
The lord has arrived;
blessings and emoluments have gathered together …
